"Knights are wizards sworn to grow their power and protect the Triplanets from chaos and demons."
"They rank above all regular wizards; not always the strongest, but never weak."
"A knight may not break the sacred promise, and knights are not family to one another."
"Fighting a knight means execution by beheading, even for the winner."
"Knights carry ordinal titles: the Primary, the only one and most powerful, then secondary, tertiary."
"The Primary's role is something like a cross between a nuclear warhead and the Pope."
"Artonans say brave matters more than strong for a knight."
"Worli Ro-den calls knighthood a terrible life for crazy wizards and idiots."
"Knights are the Triplanets' first line of defense, so high-ranked humans are rarely sent to fight."
"Knights bind their authority into skills like Avowed, but are not Avowed, and feel the binding."
"A knight funnels power into one well-designed, infinitely expandable skill plus a few conveniences."
"Knights wear metal studs instead of embroidery and use the System without tablets or lenses."
"A knight on duty must have a healer at all times."
"Knights may choose their rest, a final sacrifice, to escape the pain of affixation."
"The Primary releases them by holding their hands; they fall dead without a mark."
"Released knights' authority is woven into ground and forest as a ward against chaos."
"Knights once included non-Artonans, but do not recruit humans."
"Knight students wear quilted purple coats and enter training around human age twelve."
"Earth's System renders the numbered knights as Generals; the Quaternary is the Fourth General."
"Seeing a numbered knight is like sighting an endangered animal."
"Wizards are obliged to keep silent about knights outside their class."
"Knights live in Privately Governed Territories on Artona I, such as the forest Knight Rapport 1."
"Even Artonans cannot affix without swearing oaths never to harm the Triplanets."
